PREVIOUS_FAST_FORWARD: run faster than real time

PREVIOUS_FAST_FORWARD=N lets emulated time run up to N times as fast as
real time when the host keeps up ("max" for no limit).  The machine stays
consistent with itself; only its clock runs ahead of the host's, so
timings measured inside aren't a real NeXT's.

--- src/timing.c
+++ src/timing.c
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@
 
 #ifdef __MINGW32__
 #include <unistd.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #define timegm _mkgmtime
 #endif
 #include <float.h>
